<article class="env-exercise" id="02EO">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02EO">Exercise <span data-tag="02EO">111.29.1</span>.</a> Give an example of a finite type ${\mathbf Z}$-algebra $R$ with the following two properties: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
There is no ring map $R \to {\mathbf Q}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
For every prime $p$ there exists a maximal ideal ${\mathfrak m} \subset R$ such that $R/{\mathfrak m} \cong {\mathbf F}_ p$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>